## What Cline did most recently (June 13 2026)

### Hero responsive layout overhaul + image focal point system + mobile scrim fix

- **tokens.css (hero wrapper)** — changed `.ov-hero-wrapper` to full-width with 20px left/right margin at all viewports < 1840px. At ≥ 1840px, caps at max-width 1680px centered. Removed hero from container padding system — hero now has its own independent layout.
- **tokens.css (mobile scrim)** — changed `.ov-hero-scrim` mobile gradient from `175deg` to `0deg` (straight top-to-bottom) at ≤ 720px.
- **Hero.jsx** — added optional `imgFocus` field to each slide in `heroSlides` array (e.g. `"65% 35%"`). Background image `backgroundPosition` now uses `s.imgFocus || "center"` instead of hardcoded `"center"`. Each slide can have its own focal point.
- **PageHero.jsx** — added optional `imgFocus` prop. Image `backgroundPosition` uses `imgFocus || "center"` instead of hardcoded `"center"`. All existing callers work unchanged (fall back to `"center"`).

### How imgFocus works (explainable to client)
- Each hero image gets a focal point as `"X% Y%"` (horizontal vertical) — a CSS `background-position` value
- The percentage is relative to the container, so the same value works at every viewport width
- Desktop shows full scene; mobile crops toward the focal point keeping the subject in frame

