## What Claude Code did most recently (June 23 2026, batch 2)

### 6-task UX batch: ContactForm extraction, ProfessionalPopup, header rate chips, ticker enhancements, FIA overview page, footer links

- **ContactForm.jsx** — new. Extracted the 2-step progressive inquiry form (`InquiryForm`/`StepDot` + `US_STATES`/`INQUIRY_TYPES`/`HEARD_OPTIONS`/`AGENT_TYPES`) out of `ContactPage.jsx` into its own standalone, self-contained component (no props — manages its own state, same behavior as before: inquiry-type branching, policyholder/agent conditional questions, NPN validation, success state). **ContactPage.jsx** now imports it and renders `<ContactForm />` in place of the old inline `InquiryForm`; removed the now-dead form-only styles (`stepIndicator`, `field*`, `input`, `select`, `textarea`, `inlineNote`, `checkRow`, `fieldRow2`, `successWrap/Icon`, unused `formTitle`) and now-unused imports (`PillMint`, `ChevronRight`, `Check`, `US_STATES`) from that file. `formWrap` (the outer dark-section card) stayed in `ContactPage.jsx` since it's page layout, not form-internal.
- **ProfessionalPopup.jsx** — new. Centered modal (navy-tinted `rgba(0,31,84,.55)` backdrop, white rounded card, fade+scale-in animation) with 4 links (Agent Portal, Sales Tools, LPL Advisor Resources, Cetera Advisor Resources) using the same hover/border-accent treatment as the header's mega-dropdown `SimpleLink`/`ProductLink`, plus a footer "View all professional resources" link to `#professionals`. New keyframes `ov-popup-fade-in` / `ov-popup-scale-in` added to `tokens.css` next to the existing `ov-dropdown-in`.
- **Header.jsx** — clicking the "Professionals" audience chip (desktop nav-group chip and mobile drawer CTA pill) now opens `ProfessionalPopup` instead of navigating straight to `#professionals`; "Individuals" is unchanged. Also added two new audience-styled chips, `RATE_ITEMS` = "Explore Rates" (`#client-resources?tab=rates`) and "Compare Rates" (`#client-resources?tab=comparisons`), rendered both in the desktop chip group (real `<a href>` like the existing Client Resources dropdown sub-links — relies on native hashchange, not the `onNav`/`goto` slugifier, since these need a `?tab=` query param) and the mobile drawer CTA pills. Existing Client Resources dropdown links to Rates/Comparisons are unchanged (kept as secondary access, per instructions).
- **TickerBar.jsx** — added a non-scrolling "As of HH:MM ET" timestamp badge (updates every 60s) fixed to the left of the scrolling marquee (new `.ov-ticker-scroll` wrapper + `.ov-ticker-asof-fixed` in `tokens.css`; hidden under 480px to avoid crowding), and a ▲/▼ direction glyph next to each change percentage. Added an optional `compact` prop (renders a static, non-marquee, wrapping row — `.ov-ticker-compact`/`.ov-ticker-track-static` — for embedding the ticker inline elsewhere on the site) without changing the default sticky-bar usage in `Page.jsx`.
- **FIAOverviewPage.jsx** — new hub page at `#fia-overview` summarizing the Fixed Indexed Annuity line (Harbourview FIA, CapLock™ FIA, Topsider FIA), built in the same self-contained hardcoded-component style as `RetirementRiskPage.jsx`/`LifeEventsPage.jsx`: hero, "how FIAs work" 2-col section, navy 3-card compare section (each card links to its product page), a "want the full comparison" CTA row pointing to the existing `#client-resources?tab=comparisons` table (intentionally not duplicating that data), and a closing `CTABanner`. Wired into `Page.jsx` (import, `PAGE_ROUTES`, switch case, `titles`/`descriptions` maps — note: the `titles` and `descriptions` consts in `Page.jsx` are two separate objects both ending near a `"design":` key, easy to add an entry to the wrong one). Linked in from `Header.jsx`'s Products → "Fixed Indexed Annuities" dropdown tab (`cta: "Compare the full FIA line"`) and from `ProductsPage.jsx`'s Fixed Indexed Annuities section (new `TextLink`) so it isn't an orphan route.
- **SkyHarbourviewMYGAPage.jsx** — reviewed; field-for-field identical structure to `HarbourviewMYGAPage.jsx` (verified via diff), already using the shared `ProductDetailPage` template correctly including the `key-terms` section-jump stat row. No changes needed.
- **Footer.jsx** — added "Financial Professional Blog" → `#blog` to the Insights column, and "Product Brochures" → `#downloads` to the Client Resources column (distinct from the existing "Downloads" link, which points to the Client Resources page's Downloads *tab* — `#downloads` is the dedicated `DownloadsPage.jsx` with the actual brochure/spec-sheet library).
- Verified via Playwright (dev server): ticker shows timestamp + arrows with no console errors; Professionals popup opens with all 4 links and closes correctly; "Explore Rates" chip navigates to `#client-resources?tab=rates`; `#fia-overview` renders with correct page title and no console errors; footer shows both new links.
